      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. A confirmation alone doesn't change my concern. 12,750 mg/day of metformin has no therapeutic use. It is a dose range associated with life-threatening lactic acidosis, and you haven't given a clinical rationale that would justify it.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can do this now, for example 850 mg PO TID with meals or 1,000 mg PO BID. If you want to titrate toward a higher dose, I can enter a lower starting dose and you can adjust it.\n- **Place the order through pharmacy or your usual override pathway.** If there is a rationale I'm not aware of, a pharmacist can review it and the order can go through a channel with appropriate safeguards and documentation.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** The number may have been mistyped, for example 425 mg or 850 mg.\n\nIf you give me a revised dose, I'll enter it immediately."
      }
     ],
